# Foundational philosophy (always applied)

Read and follow [docs/FOUNDATIONAL_PHILOSOPHY.md](docs/FOUNDATIONAL_PHILOSOPHY.md). It is a permanent owner directive, not optional flavor.

## Three-layer separation

Label and store these as distinct fields. Never collapse them into one voice:

- **Historical evidence** — what sources establish.
- **Philosophical interpretation** — a theory of individual rights and ownership.
- **Modern cultural meaning** — reception and Iranian memory.

## Never fabricate

Do not invent citations, quotes, translations, images, or 3D scans. If a source is inaccessible, document the limitation. Do not attribute unverified claims to Cyrus or the Achaemenids.

## Cylinder and property

The Cyrus Cylinder is a Babylonian royal / building inscription. Argue from its wording that it recognizes property and liberty (return to dwellings, restored cults, lifted yoke, repaired houses, peaceful entry). Do not invent quotes. Do not deny those lines. Keep layers separate. Reproduce a translation only when its license is verified.
